**Final results** — T2tt_800_400 compressed signal region, 35.9 fb⁻¹ at √s=13 TeV:

| MET bin [GeV] | Expected yield |
|---|---|
| [250, 350) | 1.7381 |
| [350, 450) | 1.5428 |
| [450, 550) | 0.8984 |
| [550, ∞)   | 1.4647 |
| **Total**  | **5.64** |

The key fix that enabled correct results was including hard-process b/c/t quarks as `status=3` particles in the HepMC3 file — without these, Delphes couldn't identify b-jets and the entire b-tagging requirement in the preselection was essentially disabled (6% efficiency → 27.7%). The ledger cross-check confirms: σ·L·BR·ε = 0.0272 pb × 35.9 fb⁻¹ × 1 × 0.00578 = 5.64 events, matching the histogram sum exactly.
